# Fair classification on an Adult-style dataset (synthetic generator
# uses ~6 features mimicking age / education / hours; if you have the
# real Adult CSV, set csv_path: <path> with feature_*, group, outcome
# columns).
#
# Demographic-parity gap is the fairness metric. Pre-shift the
# environment over-samples one group; post-shift the other. Optimal
# threshold differs by group, so an algorithm that doesn't adapt
# loses on accuracy.

name: fairness_adult
description: |
  Adult-style fair-classification bandit. Two demographic groups with
  different feature distributions and different score thresholds for
  optimal accuracy. Distribution shift = group-prevalence flip mid-run.
  Tests whether algorithms can re-find the right threshold post-shift
  while keeping the demographic-parity gap small.
horizon: 10000
n_seeds: 20
delta: 0.05

environment:
  type: FairnessBandit
  n_arms: 10
  n_features: 6
  fairness_metric: demographic_parity
  schedule: single
  shift_times: [5000]
  window: 200
  sigma: 0.05

algorithms:
algorithms:
  - PCBShift
  - Auer16
  - ParetoUCB
  - AnnealingPareto
  - Kone23
  - Cai24
  - ScalarizedUCB
  - RandomPlay

metrics:
  - PreferenceRegret
  - HausdorffRegret
  - DominanceCoverage
  - ParetoPrecisionRecall
